// Handing a concept's items back to its main-set rows in kind order (order.id has
// the keys). The ids and the reasons travel together, because a reason describes
// the item it was written for ("expected first-try success 76%"), and every row
// whose item changed gets a note saying it was ordered by kind and which kind now
// stands there. plan_moved_text words the note ("" for a row that kept its item),
// plan_rows_write writes the new ids and reasons, and plan_order_concept does the
// whole thing for one concept: nothing happens to a concept with fewer than two
// rows in the main set.

plan_moved_text(Pack plan_pack, string plan_old_id, string plan_new_id, string plan_level, string plan_concept_id) {
  string plan_new_kind_text = pack_field(plan_pack, pack_find(plan_pack, "item", plan_new_id), "kind");
  string plan_moved = "";
  if (plan_old_id != plan_new_id) {
    plan_moved = "; ordered by exercise kind for a " + plan_level + " learner on " + plan_concept_id + " (" + plan_new_kind_text + " at this place)";
  }
} return string plan_moved;
given pack_fixture_parse("item: p\nkind: proof\nitem: e\nkind: error_hunt\n") ((import pack_fixture_book), "p", "e", "novice", "c"):("; ordered by exercise kind for a novice learner on c (error_hunt at this place)")
